mission "The Crown's True Owner"
    name "The Crown's True Owner"
    description "Present the stone record to the island councils and decide who may claim the discovery."
    source "Santa Isabela"
    destination "Crown's Fall"
    reward 2175
    speaker offer "Commodore Anne Bonny"
    speaker visit "Commodore Anne Bonny"
    speaker complete "Commodore Anne Bonny"
    to offer
        has "The Kingdom Below: done"
    on offer
        conversation
            `The stone record has been placed before the island councils. Each wants the discovery protected; each also knows that the first claimant may try to turn it into a crown's possession.`
            `Commodore Bonny waits until the room has quieted. "We have a choice now. We can let one flag claim the drowned kingdom, or make certain the discovery is held in common. I want the councils to hear the record before anyone writes a new charter around it."`
            choice
                `"I will put my ship to it. Let us get underway."`
                    accept
                `"Why ask a captain instead of going to the authorities?"`
                    goto details
                `"I would rather not have my name in these papers."`
                    close
            label details
                `Bonny leaves the record in the centre of the table. "There will be arguments. Some will ask who has the right to speak for a place under the sea; others will ask who is paying to keep it secret. Keep the record in view and let the councils decide together."`
                choice
                    `"Agreed. Let us make certain the truth reaches daylight."`
                        accept
                    `"I have decided. I will not be sailing."`
                        close
    on accept
        log "Accepted The Crown's True Owner. Present the stone record to the island councils and decide who may claim the discovery."
    on visit
        conversation
            `At Crown's Fall, Bonny presents the stone record to the island councils. They agree that no single crown or company may claim the discovery. "It belongs to the sea and the people around it," she says. "We must decide its future together."`
    on complete
        conversation
            `Bonny rests a hand on the closed record. "You have helped prevent a new war over an old secret. A discovery is not a prize simply because someone reaches it first. Let the councils keep the record, and let the people decide what it means."`
        log "Completed The Crown's True Owner. Received 2175 gold. Present the stone record to the island councils and decide who may claim the discovery."
